Z||000000||Lonespud||04-29-99||04:44 PM||||I just purchased an 84 Fiero for $100.00.  the body and interior are in good shape but it has a blown engine.  I think it has the 2.5 4 cyl engine.  What other engines could I install in this car without replacing any other parts?
Z||000001||PaUL||04-29-99||04:51 PM||||without replacing any other parts? pretty much none. All engine swaps would require lots of additional parts like the exhaust, mounts, alternator/AC brackets, so on. Your cheapest bet would be to find a 2.8 V6 out of a fiero and get the exhaust, mounts, computer, and others. This means all the parts in the engine compartment.
Z||000002||Shipbuilder||04-29-99||04:58 PM||||If you don't want to rebuild your engine, Advance Auto sells remanufactured engines. 4 cyl. 2.5L for a Fiero $1075 plus $200 core charge. Priced it out about 2 weeks ago. I pick up my block, head, crank etc... from the machine shop tomorrow. Had to have it bored out. By the way, I paid $200 for mine.  Have fun.
